WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
On a visit, you usually only mention what's wrong.

2
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.770
So Quickler automatically assumes anything you don't mention is OK.

3
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.500
Quickler reads each question to work out whether a place might

4
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.840
simply not have it.

5
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.840
For example, if your report asks about solar panels, most buildings

6
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.600
don't have them, so if they're not mentioned, Quickler marks them as not applicable.

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.520
And of course, you can always change any answer in the Record afterwards.
